# Project standards

- Follow `docs/PROJECT_STANDARDS.md` for all product work.
- Treat `project/` only as a Figma visual reference; never modify it or ship code from it.
- Implement frontend only in `frontend/` with React JSX, and backend only in `backend/` with Node.js JavaScript. Use npm only.
- Follow the visual design system in section 11: approved palette, Be Vietnam Pro, JetBrains Mono for data, 8px spacing grid, fixed type scale, responsive layout and shared component states.
- Do not add arbitrary colors, fonts, spacing, radii, duplicated inline styles or visual effects that diverge from the Figma reference.
- Rebuild Figma screens from reusable frontend primitives. Pages compose features and must not call HTTP APIs directly.
- Backend routes stay thin; use shared validation, error mapping, authorization/scope middleware, audit, transactions and domain policies. Controllers do not access Prisma directly.
- Validate on both client and server. Server-side permissions, state transitions, prices, entitlements, capacity and time rules are authoritative.
- Keep Swagger/OpenAPI, tests and the matching FE/API integration in the same MVP-group change set.
- Never edit applied Prisma migrations, commit secrets, add mocks to a delivered flow, or bypass a failing quality gate.
- Apply the mandatory one-group delivery loop in `mvp-delivery-loop.mdc` before moving to another MVP group.
